From 9a48f7aad08615ad4cd4e19e52a7986c121a3b78 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 23:28:20 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] presentation: super-sampled textures, Anime4K detail mix,
 deband edge guard, blended button prompts

- paraLLEl-GS super_sampled_textures on (GA2_PGS_SS_TEXTURES=0 disables), so
  2D scenes composed off-screen keep their internal-resolution detail.
- Anime4K at 2x/4x runs on a box-downscaled picture and mixes the full-resolution
  frame back in where it has detail the small picture lost (text, icons).
- Debanding reads its setting by value, defaults to Low, and skips pixels near
  strong edges so text stays sharp.
- HD button prompts fill the original icon's spot by interpolating its border
  instead of a flat average colour.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
